1. Make a very thin smear of the material on a clean grease-free glass slide, Dry in air,
3. Fix the smear by flaming the slide.
4. Add gentian violet to cover the smear and leave undisturbed for 1 minute.
5. Drain off the gentian violet by tilting the slide and rinse in flowing tap water taking care that the water flow does not directly fall on the smear.
6. Add Gram's iodine solution to cover the smear and leave for 1 minute.
7. Rinse with water in the same way as above.
8. Flood with acetone for about 30 seconds.
9. Rinse again with water.
10.Counter stain with safranin for 30 seconds, and rinse in water.
11.Dry in air and observe.
