Urea hydrolysis- The Christensens urea agar is recommended and is prepared according to the manufacturer instructions.
Using a loop inoculate a small amount of the yeast colony on the agar surface.
Inoculate appropriate control (C.albicans - negative control, C. neoformans - positive control).
Incubate the slant at 25 degree C for 2-5 days.
A deep pink color indicates a positive test.
Rapid urea hydrolysis.
The rapid urea hydrolysis test is done in microtitre plates and used to screen for C. neoformans.
Dispense 3-4 drops into each well of the microtiter plate.
Transfer a heavy inoculum of freshly isolated colony of yeast into urea broth into a well.
Seal the plate with a tape and incubate for 4 hours at 37 degree C.
Pink to red color is positive test.
Similarly inoculate the controls, C. neoformans as positive control and C. albicans or uninoculated well as negative control.
It can be used to distinguish C. neoformans from other species of Cryptococcus and C. dubliniensis from C. albicans.
Incubate one tube at 37 degree C and other at 25 degree C.
Examine the tube everyday up to 4-7 days for the presence of growth.
Growth must be present in both the tubes before concluding that the yeast has the ability to grow at 37 degree C.
Canavanine Glycine Bromothymol Blue Agar (CGB) Test.
This test is used to differentiate between C. neoformans from C. gattii.
The latter hydrolyses glycine to form ammonia to alter the pH of the medium towards alkalinity and thus change its color to blue while the former does not.
Canavanine acts as a selective agent.
Prepare CGB agar slants in tubes.
Inoculate surface of the slant using minimum inoculum of C, neoformans or C gattii with a straight wire loop.
Put a positive control (C gattii) and negative control (C.neoformans) simultaneously.
Incubate at 25 C for 1 - 5 days.
At the end of 5 days positive result is shown by color change from greenish yellow (pH 5.8) to cobalt blue (pH 7.0).
Cryptococcus neoformans when grown on the medium containing bird seed agar produces dark brown or black colonies containing melanin.
Prepare birdseed agar (BSA) (Guizotia abyssinica / Niger seeds) or Caffeic acid agar in the test tube.
Incubate the media at 25 - 30 C and observe every day up to one week.
C. neoformans produces dark brown or black colonies with in 3-5days of inoculation.
