Rinse the MALDI target plate with deionized water and wipe it dry with a Kimwipe.
If the cleaned MALDI target plate is not immediately used, store it in the plastic storage box.
Select the MALDI Biotyper Methods (MSPs from Libraries/ MSPs from Taxonomy Trees) and click Next.
Emulsify one loop-full of fresh culture in 1 mL sterile DDW in 1.5 mL microcentrifuge tube.
Centrifuge the suspension at 13,000 rpm for 2 minutes.
Discard the supernatant and repeat steeps 1 to 4 twice.
Spot 1 L of this suspension in duplicate on the MALDI plate and dry in air.
Overlay the spots with 0.5 L of 98% formic acid and again air dry it.
Added 0.8 L of matrix solution on each spot.
Identify each dried spot by MALDI-TOF MS.
The spectra will be acquired by FLEX control software and the spectra will be matched against the existing database present in MALDI Biotyper software.
