Inoculate fungal growth in 5 mL of Sabouraud dextrose broth in 15 mL centrifuge tube.
Spin the tubes in a test tube rotator at 50 rpm for 12 -24 hours at 28 C.
Keep the tubes in static condition for 10 minutes for sedimentation of hyphal flakes.
Transfer 1.5 mL of suspension in to a microcentrifuge tube by using blunt-end pipettete tips.
Centrifuge at 13,000 rpm for 5 minutes.
Completely remove the media.
Add 1.5 mL sterile DDW for washing the pellet.
Remove 1.2 mL supernatant and replace with 700 L absolute ethanol and keep for 5 minutes.
Remove the ethanol content by pipetteting and vacuum concentrator.
Incubate at room temperature for 5 minutes.
Add 50-80 L acetonitrile (ACN).
Vortex the emulsion for 5 -10 minutes with 0.5 mm acid-washed glass beads for proper lysis.
Centrifuge at 10,000 rpm for 5 minutes.
Overlay the dry spot was with 1 L matrix solution.
Air dry prior to MALDI-TOF MS analysis.
