Culture the isolates on SDA and incubate for 3 to 7 days at 28C.
Harvest very small pieces of mycelial growth by using teasing needle and place in 1.5 mL DDW in 2 mL microcentrifuge tube.
Vortex well to disperse the mycelial clump and produce thin and smaller structure.
Centrifuge it for 10 minutes at 13,000 rpm.
Completely remove the supernatant and replace with 1 mL of 70% ethanol.
Incubate at room temperature for 5 minutes.
Centrifuge the suspension at 13,000 rpm and discarded the supernatant.
Dry the pellet properly in a vacuum concentrator (Savant DNA SpeedVac Concentrator, Thermo Fisher Scientific, USA).
Add an equal amount of ACN.
Add 0.5-0.75 mm sterile acid washed glass beads (Sigma-Aldrich, Saint Quentin Fallavier, France) and vortex vigorously for 10-15 minutes.
