Wheat requires a moderate cool climate with moderate rain.
It needs temperature 10 degree C to 15 degree C for its cultivation.
It thrives well in an average temperature of 16-degree C.
Warm and sunny weather is essential at the time of ripening.
Wheat requires a rainfall of 50 cm to 100 cm during the growing season.
On irrigated lands, a rainfall of 40 cm to 50 cm is sufficient but too much rain is injurious to the plant.
Alluvial level plains are ideal for wheat cultivation but Slightly rolling plains are also suitable.
Plains should be well drained so that water cannot stand there.
Wheat requires fertile alluvial soil which should retain moisture.
Clay loamy soils or even black cotton soils are suitable.
A certain amount of lime in the soil is beneficial.
Labor factors are not as important in the wheat cultivation as in the case of rice.
