"The pericarp of the fruit is fused with the seed coat referred to as ""caryopsis"", typical of the grasses, and the entire kernel is often referred to as the ""seed""."
The grains are about the size of peas, and adhere in regular rows around a white, pithy substance, which forms the ear (maximum size of kernel in subspecies is reputedly 2.5 cm/1 in [17]).
An ear commonly holds 600 kernels.
