Visit the Tomb of the Sufi Saint, Khwaja Moinuddin Chisti, and the Dargah Sharif.
The Bikaner city is bolstered by the imposing walls and has a 16th century fort housing old palaces, temples and a mosque.
Founded by Raja Rai Singh, the fort is distinguished by its long range of 37 pavilions, a line of balconies and aerial windows of varying designs.
Drive through the famous Gajner Wild Life Game Sanctuary where you can see and photograph Black Bucks, Chinkaras, Wild Boars, Blue Bulls and other animals in large herds.
Gajner Lake is surrounded by Palaces.
