In deaths occurring in road accidents 75 % direct - indirect role is of chest wound .
Neither is there a well founded arrangement for taking person injured in road accident to hospital and nor do the paramedics have the experience of taking injured people safely to the hospital without harming .
In about 70 percent injuries of chest facture occurs in ribs .
At the same time muscles of chest get damaged .
In about 80 percent people lungs get seriously damaged along with occurrence of rib fracture .
As a result of this blood and air fill up inside the chest .
Filling up of air inside chest is called pneumothorax while filling up of blood is called hemothorax .
If both these conditions are not treated immediately then in 80 percent cases there is a chance of death of a patient .
Therefore on occurrence a chest injury one should begin treatment under the surveillance of an experienced thoracic surgeon or danger increases .
Often in road accidents many ribs break together in many places .
In medical terms it is called ` flail chest ` or swinging chest .
It makes its independent identity .
Flail chest does not contribute with the original chest in the process of breathing rather it works opposite to the original chest .
If ` flail chest ` is not treated properly right away then death is certain .
In such a condition what the family members of injured person need is that they take patient to a modern hospital equipped with all modern facilities and get an experienced thoracic surgeon to treat patient .
It is dangerous to not do right treatment of ribs .
People do not take fracture of ribs seriously .
Considering it an ordinary injury they get treatment in small clinics or hospitals .
People do not understand this that the person whose rib has fractured his lung must be definitely injured slightly or in more amount .
Consequently we pay more attention to rib injury rather than lung injury and overlook lung injury .
