According to a new research done in Sweden , those men who are not able to express their anger in response to the wrong behavior against them in office , they have twice more chances of having heart attack .
In order to reach this conclusion researchers observed such 2 , 775 men employees of Stockholm , who never had heart attack .
These employees were asked in what way do they fight the anger related to the work .
Do they express their anger or remain silent .
Does headache or stomach ache start after the anger .
These employees were also asked regarding their habit of intoxication - like intake of liquor and smoking , disease ( especially diabetes ) work pressure etc .
Besides this the blood pressure , body mass index and cholesterol level of people involved in the study were also noted down .
The average age of all people included in the study was 41 years , when the study was started in between 1992 and 1995 .
The conclusion of the study that ran till 2003 was that those men who were good at tackling the current situation , in comparison to them , those men who used to hide the anger they had twice more danger of heart attack or dying by the heart disease .
