In a borrowed pregnancy or surrogacy in English , the eggs taken from a sterile women are fertilized with the sperm of husband through I. V. F. method .
Then the developed embryo is transplanted to the ovary of another women with a healthy womb .
The women who undergo miscarriage several times or have any inborn deficiency in their overies .
Many unsuccessful test - tube baby attempts or or those who got their ovaries operated out due to some reasons .
The surrogate mother can be the relative of the sterile mother or any acquaintance of the couple or it can be a stranger also .
If the husband can not generate sperm then this process of surrogacy can be performed by borrowing the sperm from a doner .
This case is cost effective .
She must have good health and she should not be addicted to toxic substances .
For example , the identity of the donor and the couple is kept confidential .
If the women donating eggs becomes the surrogate mother too , in this case the identity is not kept confidential .
The involved couple must be provided all expense related information by the doctor .
