A study proved that garlic has cancer resistance properties because it reduces the effect of Nitrokemine from food items and pollution .
According to a report published in the Journal of Analytical Biochemistry , nitrokemine is directly related to cancer .
There is high amount of nitrogen in vegetables , packaged food and the waste from the industry .
Around 20 % of nitrogen entering the body gets converted into nitrokemine .
So far it was believed that Vitamin C is capable to resisting nitrokemine to a great extent because it has anti - oxidant .
But the effect of garlic is seen in the recent studies .
The participants of the study were given nitrate and garlic free diet .
Then they one given a dose of sodium nitrate with a particular formula which does not get converted into a harmful element .
But poisonous elements were found in their urine test .
There were given one , three or five grams of garlic or were given 3 grams of the garlic juice .
Another group was given 500 mg of asorbic acid or vitamin C .
Both the groups were given this for next seven days and their urine sample was collected every second day .
The test reports revealed that the amount of nitrokenmine was lower in the group treated with garlic .
