Blood is an important part of life .
Primarily there are 55 percent plasma and 45 percent cells like red cells , white cells and platelets .
There are three types of protein in plasma - Albumin , Globulin and Fibrinogen and some factors for clotting of the blood also .
Its recognition is done by the protein ( antigen ) found on the surface of the outer membrane of the red cells .
If RH protein ( antigen ) are found in the red cells of people then they are called RH positive ( RH + ve ) .
95-98 percent Indians are RH positive and 2-5 percent are RH negative .
Any healthy man or woman of 18-60 years can donate blood .
The weight of a person donating blood must be more than 45 kilos .
Its amount of hemoglobin should be more than 12.5 gram .
Systolic blood pressure must be between 100-140 millimetre ( mm ) and diastolic 70-100 millimetre .
In a man for every kilo there s 65-80 mililitres ( mm ) of blood and they can donate 65-80 mililitre ( ml ) blood safely on every kilo of their weight .
You have had cold and fever ( whose reason you do not know ) .
You have had vaccination in the last 24 hours .
If you have had an abortion in the last six months or if you have been pregnant in the last twelve months or if you have been breastfeeding a child .
Blood donation happens fast and without pain .
The doctor will do your physical check for finding this that your blood is safe for other people .
In this is included your blood pressure , beat of heart , temperature of the body and check for anemia .
You will be taken to the place of blood donation , where your arm will be cleaned with an antiseptic i.e. that medicine which will do the cleaning of the place from were blood will be taken so that there is no wound there .
Some injection will be put into your arm and almost 350 millilitre blood will be taken .
For this a sterile needle ( without bacteria clean and which are use and throw ) and a bag of plastic will be used .
Remember that the fluid substances of the body are again made fully in 24 hours .
Its tests are also done for ' H.I.V. ' , Hepatitis ' B ' and ' C ' syphilis , malaria etc diseases it is kept between ( 4°C to 6°C ) in the refrigerator .
That person can again do blood donation after three months .
The biggest advantage of these parts is that the blood of one person can work for 4-5 types of patients , who have special needs .
For example a patient with anemia needs leukemia of ` red cells ` or a patient with bleeding .
Cryoprecipitate ` is especially given to a patient of ` Haemophilia ` or for some other patient of the disease of excessive bleeding .
Along with blood donation you can also give the donation of plasma .
There are many important proteins , nutritious elements and blood clotting elements which stop it from bleeding .
There is 5 litres of blood in a common man or woman from which 3 litres are plasma .
Biostatic or concentrated factor V111 this stops the blood from flowing in those people who have the disease Haemophilia ` A ` .
Immunoglobulin :- This is a special protein which protects people from infectious diseases like tetanus , chicken pox and hepatitis B .
Albumin - This proves helpful in the flowing of excess blood or in the supply of blood lost due to burning and works in the treatment of liver and kidney diseases .
Intragam P - There are antibodies in this also which increases the strength of fighting against our diseases , after ` bone marrow transplant ` and on weakness of fighting with diseases .
What happens on donating plasma .
It takes approximately 40 minutes to take plasma .
Is it safe to donate plasma .
The process of donating plasma is fully safe and skilled and trained people perform this .
The donation of plasma can be done every two or three weeks , because you get back your red cells .
There is no restriction of your donating plasma .
You can merely donate blood also .
How I can become a donator of plasma .
First time donator of plasma must have donated blood at least once in the last one year .
You being chosen for plasma donation depends on your being present there , the condition of the vessels of your blood , hemoglobin and blood group .
At the time of your first donation your age should be between 18-60 years .
You can give donation till the age of 70 years .
Your weight must be 50 kilos or more than this .
Why are voluntary blood donors liked more than professional blood donors ?
They can hide their any diseases or infection or the use of intoxicants which can not be even found out by tests .
By taking the blood of these people any patient can be in serious danger of these diseases .
Their blood is safe and trustworthy .
If you have fast requirement of blood then the hospital will provide you blood .
Most hospitals meet the blood given to their patients by taking from their relatives or friends .
Where do I go and donate blood ?
You can donate blood near your house , place of work or near the school by going to some blood donation camp or by going to some recognized blood donation center ( blood camp ) .
Please take information by contacting the blood bank of some local Indian Red Cross .
