Agriculture is a process of making best use of earth resources by humans for the fulfillment of initial objectives such as food, fodder, fiber, fuel etc.
The development of agriculture in the world began before 1000 BC, whose short description(till 20C mid) exists.
The development of agriculture in India- India proves its claim of being an agriculture dominant country with its consistently increasing production and has achieved major place in the world in the field of agricultural development.
Still around 17.6 % share of national income is achieved through agriculture and it is true that around 65-70 % population of our country is associated with agriculture for livelihood.
Not only this in fact every citizen of the country is directly or indirectly associated with agriculture.
The major job of the population spending life in villages in agriculture only.
`` Dasyu killing `` was a term given to the encounter of Aryans and tribals after their invasion to India and settling in eastern Afghanistan, north-western border states, Kashmir, Punjab, some parts of Sindh and Rajasthan.
The oldest religious book of the Aryans speak about the food habit of the Aryans which mentions the use of milk, ghee, vegetables etc.
The tradition of eating sheep and goat ` s meat was also there.
There are 21 references of agriculture in the Rigveda.
