Agro-forestry plays an important role in making agriculture sustainable which is proved by the research done in recent years.
The soil fertility has reduced because of adopting dense methods, not adopting proper crop cycle, blindly spraying of chemicals, soil erosion. The influence of nutrients over crop production has reduced, production has become stable.
Hence Agro forestry is a good alternative in such situations, especially in increasing production and maintaining ecology balance.
Therefore certainly it can be said that there adoption of agro-forestry is extremely important and there is good scope for it in the future.
